		new(EarlyModernHouseholdCatalogueFamily.Furniture, "earlymodern_furniture_eng_linen_press_01", "press", "an english and british stuart-georgian plain teak linen press", "An english and british stuart-georgian plain teak linen press is positioned here, its teak form giving the room a practical period presence.", "The english and british stuart-georgian plain teak linen press is made chiefly from teak, with a proportioned silhouette and carefully fitted edges. The grain of the teak is left visible across the boards, rails, or woven members. The upright body is broken into doors, panels, or shelves, with a firm plinth keeping the stored contents above the floor. Small changes in sheen around the joins make the individual pieces of the construction easy to read, with turned timber, compact brass fittings, and practical domestic proportions carried through the final detailing.", SizeCategory.Large, ItemQuality.Standard, 22000.0, 20.0m, "teak", ["Era / Early Modern Era", "Functions / Household Items / Household Furniture", "Market / Household Goods / Standard Furniture", "Functions / Container", "Culture / Early Modern / Shared / English British Stuart Georgian"], ["Destroyable_Furniture", "LockingContainer_PreIndustrial_LargeCabinet"], "Early Modern household catalogue; culture admission eng (English and British Stuart-Georgian)."),
